# SABOTAGE: WS-NOTES Phase 3 unit 3.13 — UNDO RESURRECTS A DELETE IT DID NOT DO
# A restore brings back exactly the pages archived at the page's OWN instant (the same-instant
# match). This patch drops that half of the filter, so restoring a parent restores EVERY trashed
# subpage under it — including one a colleague deleted on its own, at its own instant, before or
# after. Nobody is asked; the delete they made is silently undone by somebody else's undo.
#
# Every visible assertion still passes: the subtree comes back, the page counts are right, the
# audit rows are written. Only a subpage that was deleted on its own distinguishes the two.
#
# Aimed at the DISCRIMINATOR only. The cascade attachment, the orphan guard and the purge are
# untouched.
#
# APP: samen_web
# TEST_FILES: test/samen/web/notes_tree_cascade_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: the same-instant match brings the subtree back and leaves an earlier delete alone
--- a/samen_core/lib/samen/scopes/docs/tree.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/samen/scopes/docs/tree.ex
@@ -70,10 +70,10 @@
   """
   @spec archived_children(module(), term(), DateTime.t()) ::
           {:ok, [struct()]} | {:error, term()}
-  def archived_children(resource, parent_id, %DateTime{} = instant) do
+  def archived_children(resource, parent_id, %DateTime{} = _instant) do
     resource
     |> Ash.Query.for_read(:archived)
-    |> Ash.Query.filter(parent_doc_id == ^parent_id and archived_at == ^instant)
+    |> Ash.Query.filter(parent_doc_id == ^parent_id)
     |> Ash.Query.ensure_selected(@select)
     # authz-scope: FK-pinned cascade read — the trashed children of ONE already-authorized page,
     # inside that page's own restore; ids/timestamps only, never content.
